expected_issues.description:
`fileExistsFunction` and `fileEmptyFunction` are registered unconditionally. While they are `@Singleton`, this still assumes the beans are always present and that `Extension` is always DI-managed. For consistency with `render*` and `errorLogs`, consider either:
- Fail fast with a clear message if injection somehow results in null (e.g., `Objects.requireNonNull(fileExistsFunction, "...")`), or
- Mark them `@Nullable` and register conditionally.

This prevents a hard-to-debug NPE during template engine initialization if wiring/classpath changes in some distributions.

```suggestion
        functions.put("randomInt", new RandomIntFunction());
        functions.put("randomPort", new RandomPortFunction());
        functions.put("fileExists", java.util.Objects.requireNonNull(fileExistsFunction, "fileExistsFunction bean is missing"));
        functions.put("fileEmpty", java.util.Objects.requireNonNull(fileEmptyFunction, "fileEmptyFunction bean is missing"));
```

